{
    "id": 103,
    "title": "Paid backups by override; web search falls to Brave",
    "why": "decisions/0163's source map, step 3 (Jason, 2026-11-17: \"we can have an override for this if we need a source and no free ones are available\"; \"go on c\"). 1. Two paid backups, each off until a director sets its monthly cap in Thresholds & gates (0 = off; every change kept there with who and when; shown on the Service register under Google and Anthropic): \"Paid backup: Google Places confirms a business\" (checks a month) and \"Paid backup: Claude reads pages when Gemini can't\" (dollars a month). 2. Google Places is used by the crawler's second look at a new find (W1) and its identity check of a listing (W2), only when its own website, NPI and the web searches found nothing, at most 3 a run; only Google's Maps link goes back, never its details. On a new find it's a reference that raises its confidence (Verify kind google; Jason, 2026-11-17: \"google match is a good thing\"), and AutoImport never counts Google as a source we keep, so it can't pass the \"real business\" floor by itself; on a listing it's evidence at the confidence score's Google weight; each use is counted for the month and written to the cost ledger. 3. Page reading on Gemini: when Gemini can't answer, Claude (Haiku) reads the waiting pages while the backup's dollars last, inside the AI cap, each call kept on AI use as the backup (charged to po:prose); otherwise they wait as before. 4. The pre-flight's \"Confirm a business\" and \"Page prose into facts\" lines show the paid backup as their last source (off, on with this month's use, or at its cap). 5. The crawler (2.10.0): web search tries Tavily, then Brave when Tavily fails or is held, the switch logged and reported. No migration; no new endpoint.",
